# =============================================================================
#  Nibras environment configuration
# =============================================================================
#  Runtime audio is served as static files from public/audio/ (SHA-256-hashed
#  WAV files, committed to git, deployed via GitHub Pages). No cloud storage
#  credentials are needed for the app to run.
#
#  The only environment secret used at build time is the Gemini API key, which
#  lives in server/.env (used by scripts/cache-event-*.js to pre-generate
#  narration WAVs). Copy this stanza to server/.env and fill in a real key:
#
#     GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
#
#  Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
#  Chat assistant (api/chat.ts) — deployed as its own, separate Vercel
#  project, NOT part of the GitHub Pages static deploy. Set these as
#  server-side Environment Variables in that Vercel project's dashboard
#  (never prefix them VITE_ — that would expose them to the client bundle).
#  For local development, put them in a git-ignored .env.local and run
#  `vercel dev` from the repo root.
# =============================================================================
#     GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key_here
#     OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your_openrouter_api_key_here
#     GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here   # query embeddings for semantic search
#
#     # Optional — falls back to a sensible default chain if unset.
#     # Format: "platform:model,platform:model,...", tried in order.
#     LLM_PROVIDER_CHAIN=groq:openai/gpt-oss-120b,groq:qwen/qwen3.6-27b,groq:openai/gpt-oss-20b,openrouter:google/gemma-4-31b-it:free
#
#     # Comma-separated origins allowed to call the chat API (CORS).
#     ALLOWED_ORIGIN=https://mdshash.github.io,http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:5173
#
#  Get a Groq key at https://console.groq.com/keys
#  Get an OpenRouter key at https://openrouter.ai/keys
#
#  The frontend needs to know where this function is deployed — this one IS
#  safe to expose (it's a public URL, not a secret), so it uses the VITE_
#  prefix and lives in the repo root .env (or your shell) at build time:
#
#     VITE_CHAT_API_URL=https://<your-vercel-project>.vercel.app/api/chat
# =============================================================================
